                  html: "<p><strong>Five taps from the start screen to a report Quality can act on.</strong> The scanner reads by itself; the ERP answers; the assistant fills the form; the worker checks and submits.</p><ul><li><strong>Tap 1, scan.</strong> The viewfinder reads the label; no spinner, straight to the item context.</li><li><strong>Tap 2, report.</strong> Location and quantity stand confirmed by the same tap, so the worker does not confirm twice.</li><li><strong>Tap 3, photo.</strong> Taking it is not counted. Voice or text are the alternatives.</li><li><strong>Tap 4, the hold.</strong> Propose batch hold is already proposed by the assistant; the worker keeps it or not.</li><li><strong>Tap 5, submit.</strong> The confirmation names the number, the recipient, and the batch status.</li></ul>",
                  video: { src: `${W2}/clips/from-scan-to-action.mp4`, poster: `${W2}/clips/from-scan-to-action.webp`, title: "Flow 1 played through: scan, context, photo, review, confirmation", mockup: true },
